  "estimatedMinutes": 3,
  "statement": "What is the value of\n\n\\[ \\sum_{n=2}^{255} \\frac{\\log_2\\left(1 + \\frac{1}{n}\\right)}{(\\log_2 n)(\\log_2(n+1))}? \\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(1 - \\dfrac{1}{\\log_2 255}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{8}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{16}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "7/8"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2025-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(a_n = \\log_2 n.\\) The numerator equals \\(a_{n+1} - a_n,\\) so each term is \\(\\dfrac{a_{n+1} - a_n}{a_n a_{n+1}} = \\dfrac{1}{a_n} - \\dfrac{1}{a_{n+1}}.\\) Telescoping from \\(n = 2\\) to \\(255\\) leaves \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\log_2 2} - \\dfrac{1}{\\log_2 256} = 1 - \\dfrac{1}{8}\\) \\(= \\dfrac{7}{8}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(\\log_2\\!\\left(1 + \\frac{1}{n}\\right)\\) \\(= \\log_2(n+1) - \\log_2 n\\)",
        "With \\(a_n = \\log_2 n,\\) each term becomes \\(\\dfrac{1}{a_n} - \\dfrac{1}{a_{n+1}}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
